          "id": "c6-l1-e6",
          "type": "order_lines",
          "prompt": "Put the lines in order: print the squares of 1 to 3.",
          "lines": [
            "int main() {",
            "    int i;",
            "    for (i = 1; i <= 3; i++)",
            "        printf(\"%d\\n\", i * i);",
            "    return 0;",
            "}"
          ],
          "answer": [
            "int main() {",
            "    int i;",
            "    for (i = 1; i <= 3; i++)",
            "        printf(\"%d\\n\", i * i);",
            "    return 0;",
            "}"
          ],
          "explanation": "Declare i, then the for line, then the body it repeats."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "c6-l2",
      "title": "Loops in Loops",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "A loop can run inside another loop. For every round of the outer loop, the inner loop runs completely.",
        "Use different counter names, usually i for the outer and j for the inner loop.",
        "Nested loops print tables and patterns, and walk through every pair of things."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "#include <stdio.h>",
          "",
          "int main() {",
          "    int i, j;",
          "    for (i = 1; i <= 3; i++) {",
          "        for (j = 1; j <= i; j++)",
          "            printf(\"*\");",
          "        printf(\"\\n\");",
          "    }",
          "    return 0;",
          "}"
        ],
        "output": [
          "*",
          "**",
          "***"
        ]
      },
      "exercises": [
        {
          "id": "c6-l2-e1",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "An outer loop runs 4 times, an inner loop 5 times. How often does the inner body run?",
          "options": [
            "20",
            "9",
            "5",
            "4"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "4 × 5 = 20."
        },
        {
          "id": "c6-l2-e2",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "In the example, why does the triangle grow?",
          "options": [
            "The inner loop runs up to i, which grows each round",
            "printf adds stars by itself",
            "j never resets",
            "It's random"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "Round 1 prints 1 star, round 2 prints 2, round 3 prints 3."
        },
        {
          "id": "c6-l2-e3",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What does this program print?",
          "code": [
            "#include <stdio.h>",
            "",
            "int main() {",
            "    int i, j;",
            "    for (i = 1; i <= 2; i++)",
            "        for (j = 1; j <= 2; j++)",
            "            printf(\"%d%d \", i, j);",
            "    printf(\"\\n\");",
            "    return 0;",
            "}"
          ],
          "options": [
            "11 12 21 22",
            "11 22",
            "12 21",
            "1 2 1 2"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "For each i, j runs through 1 and 2."
