        },
        {
          "id": "c6-l2-e5",
          "type": "find_bug",
          "prompt": "This prints only one row. Which line is wrong?",
          "code": [
            "#include <stdio.h>",
            "",
            "int main() {",
            "    int i, j;",
            "    for (i = 1; i <= 3; i++)",
            "        for (i = 1; i <= 3; i++)",
            "            printf(\"*\");",
            "    return 0;",
            "}"
          ],
          "answer": 5,
          "explanation": "The inner loop also uses i, so it ruins the outer loop's count. It needs its own variable: j."
        },
        {
          "id": "c6-l2-e6",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What does the \\n after the inner loop do in the example?",
