            "Stops the loop",
            "Nothing"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "Without it, all stars would end up on one line."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "c6-l3",
      "title": "break and continue",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "break leaves a loop right away, even if the condition is still true. Handy when you've found what you were looking for.",
        "continue skips the rest of this round and goes on with the next one.",
        "for (;;) with nothing in it loops forever. Programs like Unix servers ran that way, using break when it was time to stop."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "#include <stdio.h>",
          "",
          "int main() {",
          "    int i;",
          "    for (i = 1; i <= 10; i++) {",
          "        if (i % 3 == 0)",
          "            continue;",
          "        if (i > 7)",
          "            break;",
          "        printf(\"%d \", i);",
          "    }",
          "    printf(\"\\n\");",
          "    return 0;",
          "}"
        ],
        "output": [
          "1 2 4 5 7 "
        ]
      },
      "exercises": [
        {
          "id": "c6-l3-e1",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What does break do in a loop?",
          "options": [
            "Leaves the loop immediately",
            "Skips one round",
            "Pauses the program",
            "Restarts the loop"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "The program continues after the loop."
        },
        {
          "id": "c6-l3-e2",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What does continue do?",
          "options": [
            "Skips to the next round",
            "Leaves the loop",
            "Ends the program",
            "Repeats the round"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "The rest of the body is skipped this time."
        },
        {
          "id": "c6-l3-e3",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What does this program print?",
          "code": [
